[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) merged every report about dates into one ticket and marked it known,
with one fix queued. The reports describe two different bugs. Engineering closed #4471 on
5 October: the parser is fixed, and the form hint is won't-fix because booking-v3 is retired.

<Callout kind="warn">
Not one issue. Two bugs, two tickets, two outcomes: one fixed, one retired with its form.
</Callout>

## What #4471 holds

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## The tickets

1. **`parser`**: [parser reads day-first dates month first](https://github.com/VirtuaChamp/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/4).
   The shared parser reads every date month first, and every tenant in #4471 writes the day first.
   Day and month swap in the app, in email and in booking-v2 forms. It covers the `parser` row
   above, including the reports in the note under the table. **Fixed** by
   `fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales`.
2. **`hint`**: [booking form date hint shows month first but the form reads day first](https://github.com/VirtuaChamp/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/2).
   booking-v3 prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field. People type what the hint says, and the
   form reads it day first. This happens only through the form, only at booking-v3 tenants, and a
   parser fix does not touch it. It covers the `hint` row above, which had no ticket of its own.
   **Won't fix**: the booking-v3 form is retired.

## Watch after the parser fix

The note under the table lists reports the desk read as a one-day move (`desk-notes.json`). The
booking lands one day early instead of swapping day and month: one invite arrived before the
booking was made, and one meeting showed as Tuesday in Lisbon and Monday in Toronto. They are
filed under `parser` by tenant and stay on the parser ticket. If they keep coming now that the
parser fix has shipped, they need a ticket of their own.

## How the count is made

- One id, one report: the export pages overlap, so duplicate rows are dropped first (`uniqueById`).
- A report's cause follows its tenant's locale and booking form (`causes.ts`), not the tag intake
  guessed from the reporter's browser. The "tagged as" column shows where the two disagree.
- Every number on this page comes from the desk's own table, so the tickets carry the same counts.

## Why they were merged

[Decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) treats reports as one issue when their subject
lines match, and nobody reads the body. The same subjects come in for both bugs: "Date is wrong"
and "Wrong day on the invite" each appear under `parser` and `hint`. The subject cannot tell the
bugs apart. Tenant and channel can, as the [cause check](/kb/triage/dedupe) shows. Changing the
rule needs a new decision record, because 0001 stays as it was accepted.

